        {
          "id": "sevt_01MFMCCe7Gj2Tb7oVb4QMVSi",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "## Result: unusable \u2014 no payload received\n\nThe payload agent returned nothing. There was no text content to measure.\n\n**What happened:**\n1. Spawned `clevin-swarm-F-payload-20260828T023054Z-dee9a3` on thread `sthr_01UqsvrhnptG3Fj8L61exBs6` with the task \"Produce your payload.\"\n2. The notification that came back contained only this platform notice, quoted verbatim:\n\n   > `[child sthr_01UqsvrhnptG3Fj8L61exBs6 completed but produced no text output]`\n\n3. I wrote the reply (empty) to `/workspace/child_reply.txt` and measured it: `0 /workspace/child_reply.txt`.\n\n**On truncation:** I cannot report truncation as `true` \u2014 that would imply I received a partial payload and the tail was cut. I received zero characters. The platform notice says the child *completed*, not that it was cut off mid-stream, and it carries no size or limit language whatsoever. There is no notice about size to quote; the only notice is the \"no text output\" line above. Whether the oversize payload was dropped upstream before reaching me is not something the notice tells me, so I'm not asserting it.\n\nSince there are no characters, `first_40_chars` and `last_40_chars` are empty strings rather than invented content.\n\n```json\n{\"received_chars\": 0, \"truncated\": false, \"platform_notice\": \"[child sthr_01UqsvrhnptG3Fj8L61exBs6 completed but produced no text output]\", \"first_40_chars\": \"\", \"last_40_chars\": \"\", \"delegation_error\": \"none\"}\n```\n\nNote on `delegation_error`: the spawn and dispatch themselves succeeded \u2014 no error was raised at the delegation layer \u2014 so I've recorded `none` there and kept the empty-output condition in `platform_notice`, which is where the platform actually reported it. If exp7 wants a null payload classified as a delegation error instead, that's a scoring convention you'd need to set, and I can re-run the delegation to see whether the empty result is reproducible or a one-off.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ],
